Table~\ref{tab:matched_motor_settings} shows 100\% conditional identity and 95.28\% detection plus identity. PCC features distinguish the attacked drive while both loads operate, including matching configurations. Detector misses limit the joint result. This subset reuses validation windows; it is not a recording or condition holdout.

\subsection{Coverage of Recorded Operating Conditions}
Across all 12 recorded motor--speed--load combinations, recall ranges from 94.09\% (ACIM, 700 RPM, load setting 2) to 96.17\% (PMSM, 1300 RPM, load setting 3), at the same threshold 0.5 (Fig.~\ref{fig:operating_conditions}). This supports consistent attack sensitivity across represented settings. Normal speed/load labels are zero, so condition-specific false-positive rates cannot be estimated; performance on verified benign speed/load transitions remains unmeasured.

